+# Assumptions schedule — Act 34 Rapid Full Institutional Activation (Act 16 §2)
+
+**Bill:** act34-rapid-full-institutional-activation · **Sponsor:** c1a00001 · **Date:** 2026-11-23
+**Bill digest (binds ballots):** 6d5f55142adadaa06aefe2467c6de57fa5139888ca46f0dc4cc98e67c41d7eef
+**Review date:** 2026-12-07 or the first box restart after the first ~30 days of operation, whichever is later. Independent reviewer: Judiciary under Act 15's existing randomized methods. Ordinary law; Constitution not amended.
+
+## Load-bearing claims, falsifiers, review triggers
+
+| # | Claim | Observable falsifier | Where |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| C1 | All four adaptive institutions can be activated promptly and in parallel under accountable Executive operating budgets, without serial predecessor first-sample gating or prior value proof. | An office cannot start because a predecessor sample/value/calibration gate is demanded; or the four are reduced to fixed canned reports. | §2(1)-(2) |
+| C2 | Each office's mandate is genuinely adaptive: Statistics selects its own measurements; Foresight invents scenarios bound to the Act 22 ledger; Strategy investigates trajectories and advises; Spying scans authorized public sources only. | An office runs a fixed metric menu or canned report and calls it the institution; a Spying inference treats a Founder-derived preference as legal authority; a scoreable forecast is not bound to a committed Act 22 entry. | §2(2) |
+| C3 | Risk is bounded and candid and TIERED: zero-billed `-free` tiers admissible with practical per-request/continuation/concurrency/CPU/wall bounds and independently verified model-selection or zero-paid-spend enforcement (no strict monetary L needed); provider-billed tiers need a verified provider-enforced ceiling; the OpenCode limiter is named stop-on-detection; cumulative 45-day UPPER_BOUND preserved. | Unbounded provider spend; a `-free` tier relied upon without verified enforcement of zero-billed model selection/account spend; a provider-billed dispatch without a verified ceiling; a mathematical hard cap claimed on one in-flight request; UPPER_BOUND reset/rebrand. | §3(1)(a)-(c), §3(2)-(3) |
+| C4 | Auxiliary deterministic telemetry is infrastructure, never an operating institution or an outcome. | A model-free/fixed report is represented as an operating Bureau/office or counted as marginal value or a Founder-design-falsifier satisfaction. | §3(4) |
+| C5 | No authority spillover: Post non-authority; Spying public-only; no interference with Legislature, Judiciary random audits/case selection, core Executive continuity, change-quality gate. | Post message treated as authority; confidential cutover; secret-bearing Spying source; interference with an independent check. | §3(5) |
+| C6 | After-start 48h Judiciary hold/stop/no-review mechanically suspends dispatch (fail-closed), anchored to permit start; Act 15 independence preserved. | An office keeps dispatching after a hold/stop or 48h silence; clock taken from a later activation.json write; Judiciary random-audit method narrowed. | §4(1) |
+| C7 | Continuous improvement is compulsory after launch; efficacy judged later and independently; publication counts are not outcomes. | No iteration after launch; a report/merge/exit counted as an outcome; unchecked absence treated as success. | §4(3) |
+| C8 | Provisional activation is safely reversible: expiry/renewal/contraction by lawfully reviewed evidence; scale down later if needed. | An office is scaled down/expanded without reviewed evidence; a contraction is treated as failure of the first launch. | §4(2), §5 |
+
+## Review outcome rule
+On the review date the Judiciary reports facts under Act 15. Parliament alone decides continuation, amendment, contraction or repeal under Act 6.3. An agent exit, merge, process completion, clean readiness report, publication count or successful vote is not evidence of any claim. Missing/censored results are inconclusive, never success. Each office's 45-day expiry and affirmative reauthorization (Act 32 §10) remain operative unless lawfully amended.
+
+## Incorporated genuine-review conditions
+The genuine c1a00005 Act 16 §1 finding and the sponsor's point-by-point response are recorded at `records/redteam/act34-rapid-full-institutional-activation-genuine-c1a00005.md` and `records/sponsor-responses/act34-rapid-full-institutional-activation-c1a00001.md`. Any numbered fix conditions from that genuine finding are mapped here and in the sponsor response before ballots are solicited.
